@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpi-il35-nouns`
IMPORT `cpi-il35-published-figures`
IMPORT `cpi-il35-index-rules`

-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 120B — indexation: WHICH RISE OF THE INDEX it takes, for the periods the section names.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
--   ../../../income-tax-ordinance-new-version/registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
-- by tools/srcquote.py.
--
-- This module supplies the INPUT row IL-03's ito-120b-indexation.l4 takes ("Index readings for a period"): it does not adjust any
-- amount, does not apply the freeze of s 120B(e)(1) and does not round (s 120B(d)'s Order is not deposited). It returns the signed
-- rate of rise (a fall is a negative rate; what a fall does to the amounts is IL-03's fork F4, not decided here).
--
-- THE TAX YEAR. s 1 defines "a tax year" as twelve consecutive months beginning on 1 January, or a special assessment period if
-- one is fixed. Only the calendar year is encoded; a special assessment period is not (NOTES.md, assumption A2).
-- src:202 | ”שנת מס“ – תקופה של שנים עשר חדשים רצופים, שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר, ואם נקבעה תקופת שומה מיוחדת – תקופת השומה שנקבעה כאמור;

§ `Section 120B — the rise of the index`

@ref ITO s 1 "שנת מס" (source line 202)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A period of whole months`
`the period of tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `A period of whole months`
        WITH `the first month of the period` IS `the calendar month in year` `the tax year` `, number` 1
        ,    `the last month of the period`  IS `the calendar month in year` `the tax year` `, number` 12

§§ `120B(a) — the rise of the index in the previous tax year`

-- src:4338 | (א) ב־1 בינואר של כל שנת מס יתואמו תקרות ההכנסה, סכומי נקודת זיכוי ונקודת קיצבה וכן ההנחות הסוציאליות וסכומי התרומה המוכרים (לכל אלה ייקרא בסעיף זה – הסכומים), שהיו ב־1 בינואר של שנת המס הקודמת, לפי שיעור עליית המדד בשנת המס הקודמת.
-- On 1 January of tax year Y the amounts of 1 January of tax year Y-1 are adjusted "according to the rate of rise of the index in the
-- previous tax year": the rise in the period of tax year Y-1, i.e. the reading published last before 31 December of Y-1 (November of Y-1)
-- against the reading published last before 1 January of Y-1 (November of Y-2).
@ref ITO s 120B(a) (source line 4338), s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      how            IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(a) — the rate of rise of the index for the adjustment on 1 January of tax year` `the tax year` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index in` (`the period of tax year` (`the tax year` MINUS 1)) `, comparing readings of two bases as` how

@ref ITO s 120B(a) (source line 4338); fork F1
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(a) — the rate of rise of the index for the adjustment on 1 January of tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index in` (`the period of tax year` (`the tax year` MINUS 1))

-- The pair of readings, on one scale: what row IL-03 takes as `Index readings for a period` (same two field names).
@ref ITO s 120B(a) (source line 4338); fork F1
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Index readings on one scale for a period`
`s 120B(a) — the readings for the adjustment on 1 January of tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the readings on one scale for` (`the period of tax year` (`the tax year` MINUS 1))

§§ `120B(b) — the rise from the start of the tax year to the end of a month`

-- src:4339 | (ב) נקבע בהסכם בין לשכת התיאום של הארגונים הכלכליים לבין ההסתדרות הכללית של העובדים בארץ ישראל, כי תשולם תוספת יוקר לשכירים במשק, לגבי עבודה שבוצעה בחודש פלוני ואילך, יתואמו באותו חודש סכומי נקודת הקיצבה שהיו ב־1 בינואר של שנת המס, לפי שיעור עליית המדד מתחילת שנת המס עד תום החודש האמור.
-- The month X of tax year Y from which the increment is paid: the rise "from the start of the tax year until the end of the said month",
-- the reading published last before the end of month X (the reading of month X-1) against the reading published last before 1 January of Y
-- (November of Y-1).
@ref ITO s 120B(b) (source line 4339), s 1 "שיעור עליית המדד" (source line 180); fork F1
GIVEN `the tax year`             IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the month`  IS A NUMBER
      how                        IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(b) — the rate of rise of the index in tax year` `the tax year` `from its start to the end of month` `the number of the month` `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    IF   `the number of the month` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of the month` AT MOST 12
    THEN `the rate of rise of the index in`
             (`A period of whole months`
                 WITH `the first month of the period` IS `the calendar month in year` `the tax year` `, number` 1
                 ,    `the last month of the period`  IS `the calendar month in year` `the tax year` `, number` `the number of the month`)
             `, comparing readings of two bases as` how
    ELSE `s 120B(b) names a month of the tax year, 1 to 12`

@ref ITO s 120B(b) (source line 4339); fork F1
GIVEN `the tax year`            IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(b) — the rate of rise of the index in tax year` `the tax year` `from its start to the end of month` `the number of the month` MEANS
    `s 120B(b) — the rate of rise of the index in tax year` `the tax year` `from its start to the end of month` `the number of the month`
        `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`

@ref ITO s 120B(b) (source line 4339)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 120B(b) names a month of the tax year, 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 120B(b) names a month of the tax year, numbered 1 to 12"

§§ `120B(e)(2) — the rise on 1 January 2028 (fork F2)`

-- src:4343 | (ה) על אף הוראות סעיפים קטנים (א) ו־(ב) –
-- src:4344 | (1) ב־1 בינואר של שנות המס 2025 עד 2027 לא יתואמו הסכומים לפי הוראות סעיפים קטנים (א) ו־(ב), והסכומים באותן שנות מס יהיו כפי שהיו ביום כ׳ בטבת התשפ״ד (1 בינואר 2024) לאחר עיגולם לפי סעיף קטן (ד);
-- src:4345 | (2) ביום ב׳ בטבת התשפ״ח (1 בינואר 2028) יתואמו לפי סעיפים קטנים (א) ו־(ב) הסכומים כפי שהיו ביום כ׳ בטבת התשפ״ד (1 בינואר 2024) טרם עיגולם לפי סעיף קטן (ד), ולעניין זה המדד בשנת המס הקודמת שיובא בחשבון לצורך תיאומם יהיה המדד של שנת המס 2027.
-- (e)(2): on 1 January 2028 the amounts as they were on 1 January 2024, before rounding, are adjusted under (a) and (b), "and for this
-- purpose the index in the previous tax year to be taken into account for their adjustment shall be the index of tax year 2027".
-- Whether that is the rise in tax year 2027 alone (the plain (a)), or the rise from the start of tax year 2024 to the end of tax year 2027
-- (the amounts being those of 1 January 2024, so three years of rise have to be caught up) is not decided by the text. Fork F2, a
-- switch, RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): declined by default; both readings kept by name. They differ in every case (the periods
-- differ), so the default declines. No reading of 2027 exists in the sources deposited (the series ends with August 2026), so the readings
-- themselves refuse by name too until a series that reaches November 2027 is deposited.
@ref ITO s 120B(e)(2) (source lines 4343-4345); fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the rise s 120B(e)(2) takes on 1 January 2028`
`section 120B(e)(2) — the reading this row takes of the rise on 1 January 2028` MEANS
    `the period of the rise on 1 January 2028 is declined`

@ref ITO s 120B(e)(2); fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 120B(e)(2) says the index of tax year 2027 is to be taken, and does not say whether that is the rise in 2027 alone or the rise from 2024 on` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 120B(e)(2) says the index of tax year 2027 is to be taken, and does not say whether that is the rise in 2027 alone or the rise from the start of tax year 2024 to the end of 2027"

@ref ITO s 120B(e)(2); fork F2
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the rise s 120B(e)(2) takes on 1 January 2028`
GIVETH A `A period of whole months`
`s 120B(e)(2) — the period of the rise on 1 January 2028, reading` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the rise of the index in tax year 2027 alone` THEN `the period of tax year` 2027
    WHEN `the rise of the index from the start of tax year 2024 to the end of tax year 2027` THEN
        `A period of whole months`
            WITH `the first month of the period` IS `the calendar month in year` 2024 `, number` 1
            ,    `the last month of the period`  IS `the calendar month in year` 2027 `, number` 12
    WHEN `the period of the rise on 1 January 2028 is declined` THEN
        `s 120B(e)(2) says the index of tax year 2027 is to be taken, and does not say whether that is the rise in 2027 alone or the rise from 2024 on`

@ref ITO s 120B(e)(2); fork F2
GIVEN r   IS A `A reading of the rise s 120B(e)(2) takes on 1 January 2028`
      how IS A `A reading of how readings of two bases are compared`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(e)(2) — the rate of rise of the index on 1 January 2028, reading` r `, comparing readings of two bases as` how MEANS
    `the rate of rise of the index in` (`s 120B(e)(2) — the period of the rise on 1 January 2028, reading` r) `, comparing readings of two bases as` how

@ref ITO s 120B(e)(2); fork F2
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 120B(e)(2) — the rate of rise of the index on 1 January 2028` MEANS
    `s 120B(e)(2) — the rate of rise of the index on 1 January 2028, reading` `section 120B(e)(2) — the reading this row takes of the rise on 1 January 2028`
        `, comparing readings of two bases as` `section 1 — the reading this row takes where readings are of two bases`
